--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-003-reject-removal-of-the-document-root.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-reject-removal-of-the-document-root
+type: decision-log
+title: "Reject removal of the document root"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+`applyPatch` returns a JSON value. RFC 6902 specifies that the target document is a JSON document
+and defines root replacement for `add`; it provides no JSON value that represents a document after
+its root has been removed. The prior implementation silently converted that condition to `null`.
+
+## Decision
+
+Treat `remove` at the empty JSON Pointer as an unsuccessful operation and throw an error. Do not
+invent a JSON value to stand for a document with no root.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Successful calls always return the JSON document produced by RFC 6902 operations. A root `remove`
+does not report a successful application with an unrelated `null` document.
